            <ArticleTitle>[Collateral pathways in patients with univascular coronary obstruction (2)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>407-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We found 10 coronary collateral pathways in patients with right coronary (RC) obstruction. The communication with the anterior descending (DA) through the septum was the most prevalent. 5 pathways were found in the presence of DA obstruction, again the communication with the RC through the apex was the most frequently observed. Only 2 pathways were found in the presence of circumflex (Cx) obstructions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
